From: joe deras <joederasespinoza@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:02:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] platform: add d8-style predictable platform with embedder
 clock

new_predictable_platform(clock, worker_task_mode, reported_worker_threads)
creates a DefaultPlatform subclass (so v8::platform::PumpMessageLoop and
NotifyIsolateShutdown keep working) modelled on d8's PredictablePlatform:

- worker-thread tasks (CallOnWorkerThread, job workers) never run on a
  V8-owned thread: they run inline on the posting thread
  (WorkerTaskMode::Inline) or are queued until the embedder calls
  Platform::run_worker_tasks (WorkerTaskMode::Queued). Delayed worker tasks
  are queued with a due time on the platform clock.
- MonotonicallyIncreasingTime and CurrentClockTimeMillis (Date.now) come
  from a Rust PlatformClock (any Fn() -> f64 returning seconds works);
  None selects d8's synthetic counter clock. The foreground task runners
  use the same clock for delayed tasks.

V8::set_predictable_flags(seed) sets
--predictable --single-threaded --random-seed=<seed>.

